1 OCCU Capitaine de la garde pontificale de Benoît XIII, Créé Amiral de France le 22 avril 1417
1 TITL Admiral of France
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mosén Rubí de Bracamonte arrived in Santander from France by order of King Charles VI, seeking military support from King John II of Castile in the fight against the Moors. The historian Jerónimo de Zurita notes th
2 CONC at in 1401, King Henry II of Castile—known as “the one of the Gifts”—authorized him to undertake the conquest of the Canary Islands as part of diplomatic agreements between the French and Castilian crowns.
2 CONT
2 CONT After a politically active life spanning over five decades in Spain, he died in 1419 in Mocejón, near Toledo. He was buried in the main chapel of the Church of San Pedro Mártir. Later, on September 2, 1575, at the request of his g
2 CONC reat-great-grandson Diego de Bracamonte—patron of the chapel and 6th Lord of Fuente el Sol and Cespedosa—his remains were transferred, by papal decree, to the main chapel of the Convent of San Francisco in the city of Ávila.
2 CONT
2 CONT All available records confirm that the Bracamonte family originated in France and established multiple noble branches in Spain, beginning with Admiral Rubí de Bracamonte.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rubí married twice in Castile. His first wife was Inés de Mendoza, daughter of Pedro González de Mendoza and Aldonza de Ayala—ancestors of the House of Infantado. After her death, he married Leonor Álvarez de Toledo, daughter of F
2 CONC ernán Álvarez de Toledo and sister of the Lord of Valdecorneja, from whom the Dukes of Alba descend. This second marriage produced no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://historia-hispanica.rah.es/biografias/8166-mosen-rubi-de-bracamonte
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *[http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_de_Bracquemont '''Monsieur Robert, dit Robin ou Robinet de Bracquemont''] (ou de Braquemont), et Mosén Rubí de Bracamonte en espagnol (? - Mocejón, 1419), sire de Bracquemont, en Caux, et de T
2 CONC ravessain, en Normandie, amiral de France et d'Espagne est issu d’une vieille famille noble de Normandie, originaire de la vicomté d'Arques.
2 CONT *Célebre Almirante de Castilla.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Mosén Rubin DE BRACAMONTE, famoso caballero francés; con Real Licencia dada en Sevilla el 07 septiembre 1484; testó en Santander, siendo Alcaide de su fortaleza en 1518.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Robert de Bracquemont or Mosén Rubí de Bracamonte (1340s-1419) was a Norman noblemen, Admiral of France and Spain.[1]
2 CONT --------------------
