1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Doña María de Luna married Don Enrique Enríquez—uncle and *Mayordomo Mayor* (High Steward) to the Catholic King Don Fernando. He was Admiral of Sicily, Grand Commander of León, *Alcaide* (Governor) and *Alférez May
2 CONC or* (Chief Standard-Bearer) of the city of Baza, and Lord of the towns of Orce, Galera, Cortes, Sierra de Filabres, Senés, Castro, Lucainena, and Nerva; he was also the paternal half-brother of Doña Juana Enríquez, Queen of Aragon
2 CONC . *History of the Illustrious House of Sousa*, Chapter XVI: "The Great Saint Francis Borgia and his descendants, the Dukes of Gandía," p. 280.
