1 OCCU Seigneur de Sedan, Arenberg, Seraing, Aigremont, Florenville, seigneur d'Arenberg, de Neufchateau, de Lummen, d'Aigremont et de Rochefort, Sire de Sedan et de Florenville
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANCONIA%20(LOWER%20RHINE).htm#EberhardMarkdied1440 Medlands]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birthplace is Aremberg, also spelled Arenberg, is a town of Germany , in the district of Ahrweiler , in Rhineland-Palatinate
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%89vrard_II_de_La_Marck-Arenberg Wikipedia_FR]
2 CONT
2 CONT Evrard III/II Marck (in German : Eberhard III/II von der Marck-Arenberg.) ( 1365 to Aremberg - 1440 ) Lord of Sedan .  He married Marie de Braquemont, sister of Louis de Braquemont. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Member of a large noble family in Franconia , he is the grand-son of Engelbert II of Marck († 1308), Count de la Marck .  He is the son of Evrard I. and Mary of Loon, granddaughter of John I of Loon . 
2 CONT
2 CONT  He buys the 8 May 1424 , the lordship of Sedan to his brother Louis Braquemont.  He is interested in the rocky spur that dominates the small village.  It expels religious Mouzon (Ardennes) who had a priory and begins to build the
2 CONC  famous Chateau de Sedan which his son John II of Marck and Robert I of La Marck inherit. 
2 CONT
