1 NOTE Pedro I (1334-69), king of Castile and Léon, commonly surnamed "the Cruel," the only legitimate son of Alfonso XI, was born in Burgos, and succeeded to the throne in 1350. In 1353, at the instigation of his mistress, afterwards hi
2 CONC s queen, Maria de Padilla, he took the reins of government into his own hands. From that time until his death his reign was one long struggle to overthrow the power of the great vassals and to establish a strong government. [The H
2 CONC ome University Encyclopedia, 1946]
