1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/In%C3%A9s_Ayala_y_Toledo
2 CONT
2 CONT nés Ayala y Toledo
2 CONT
2 CONT Ines de Ayala y Toledo (? - September 4, 1453) IV Lady of Mount Casarrubios, Province of Toledo. She was the daughter of Pedro Suarez de Toledo II Lord of Mount Casarrubios and Juana Orozco Melendez Lady of Pinto. His remains are 
2 CONC in the Church of the Convent of Santa Isabel de los Reyes (Toledo)
2 CONT
2 CONT Political Activities
2 CONT
2 CONT Ordered the construction of the ancient palace "Casa strong", later rebuilt by Gonzalo Chacon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ines de Ayala dispossessed the Jews in the administration of any property that she thought of his noble power, to give them the Augustinian monastery, the convent of San Agustin in 1388 was moved to the site now occupied by the Sc
2 CONC hools , but respected the synagogue and their belongings, which were also his successors, Henry IV's main tax gatherers were Jews in Casarrubios. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [Edit] Descendants
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the wife of Diego Fernandez de Cordoba, Lord of Baena, this couple had a daughter: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mariana Ayala Fernandez de Cordoba (1385-1431). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maternal great-grandmother was Ferdinand. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [Edit] References
2 CONT
