2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT Álvaro de Luna y Jarana (between 1388 and 1390 – 3 July? 1453), Duke of Trujillo, 1st Count of San Esteban de Gormaz, was a Spanish politician. He was a favourite of King John II of Castile, a Constable of Castile and Grand Master
2 CONC  of the military order of Santiago.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1445, the faction of the nobles allied with Álvaro's main enemies, the Infantes of Aragon, were defeated at the First Battle of Olmedo. One of them, Infante Henry, Duke of Villena, brother of the Queen, died of his wounds. Luna
2 CONC , who had been Constable of Castile and Count of San Esteban de Gormaz since 1423, became Grand Master of the Order of Santiago by election of the Knights.
2 CONT
2 CONT Queen Maria died under suspicious circumstances, pointing to Luna as the mastermind. Nevertheless, his power appeared to be thoroughly established. It was, however, based only on the personal affection of the king. The king's seco
2 CONC nd wife, Isabella of Portugal, although her whole royal marriage was a product of Luna's arrangements, was soon offended by the immense influence of the Constable, and when the murder of the King's accountant Alfonso Pérez de Vive
2 CONC ro was suspected to have been done on Luna's orders, she urged her husband to free himself from thralldom to his favourite. In 1453 the King succumbed to his wife's demands; Luna was arrested, tried and condemned to death in a pro
2 CONC cess which was a mere parody of justice, and soon executed by beheading at Valladolid on 2 June 1453.
