2 NOTE Ferdinand II, King of Aragon, King of Castile and Léon. 
3 CONT
3 CONT Reign 20 January 1479 - 23 January 1516 
3 CONT Died 23 January 1516 (aged 63) 
3 CONT
3 CONT Ferdinand was the son of John II of Aragon (whose family was a cadet branch of the House of Trastámara) by his 2nd wife, the Castilian noblewoman Juana Enriquez. He married Infanta Isabella, the half-sister and heiress of Henry IV
3 CONC  of Castile, on 19 October 1469 in Valladolid and became jure uxoris King of Castile.
3 CONT read more about Ferinand II in his profile.
