1 OCCU VI Condestable de Castilla, Virrey de Navarra y las Provincias Vascongadas, Señor de Valdezcaray, Chief Chamerlain to King Henry iV of Castile
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (in full, Spanish: Don Pedro Fernández de Velasco y Manrique, segundo conde de Haro, sexto Condestable de Castilla, señor de los valles de Saba y Ruesga, y de las villas de Briviesca, Puebla de Arganzón, Arnedo, Me
2 CONC dina de Pomar, Santo Domingo de Silos, Salas de los Infantes, Villalpando, señor de Haro, Belorado, Frías, Villasiego y Herrera, Camarero mayor de Enrique IV de Castilla y de los Reyes Católicos, Merino mayor de Castilla la Vieja,
2 CONC  Virrey y capitán general del Reino de Navarra y de las Provincias Vascongadas) (c. 1425–1492) was a Spanish nobleman and military figure of the last stages of the Reconquista.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fernández de Velasco was born in Burgos, the son of Pedro Fernández de Velasco and of Beatriz Manrique. He became Camarero Mayor of King Henry IV of Castile, and viceroy and governor of Castile. In 1473 Henry IV named him sixth Co
2 CONC nstable of Castile and made this title hereditary in his family.
2 CONT
2 CONT He participated in the conquest of Úbeda and Baeza, which both occurred on Saint Andrew's day. He also fought against the Moors in the battles of Gibraltar and Archidona and participated in the conquest of Granada, where he died. 
2 CONC He and his wife are buried in the Capilla del Condestable in the Burgos Cathedral.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Mencía de Mendoza y Figueroa, with whom he had six children.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Bernardino Fernández de Velasco, 1st Duke of Frías, married
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Blanca de Herrera, señora de Pedraza de la Sierra
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Juana of Aragon, illegitimate daughter of Ferdinand II of Aragon.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Íñigo Fernández de Velasco, 2nd Duke of Frías, married María de Tovar, Lady of Berlanga
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Catarina de Velasco, married Pedro de Zúñiga, 2nd Count of Miranda
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Leonor de Velasco, married Juan Téllez-Girón, 2nd Count of Ureña
2 CONT
2 CONT     * María de Velasco, married
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Juan Pacheco, 1st Duke of Escalona
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Beltrán de la Cueva, 1st Duke of Alburquerque
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Isabel Fernandez de Velasco, married Juan Alonso de Guzmán, 3rd Duke of Medina Sidonia
2 CONT
