1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%8D%C3%B1igo_L%C3%B3pez_de_Mendoza_y_Luna,_2nd_Duke_of_the_Infantado
2 CONT
2 CONT Íñigo López de Mendoza y Luna (Guadalajara, 1438 – 14 July 1500) was a Spanish noble, and second Duke of the Infantado.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Diego Hurtado de Mendoza, 1st Duke of the Infantado and Brianda de Luna y Mendoza. Íñigo López de Mendoza participated in the Siege of Granada.
2 CONT
2 CONT He finished the construction on the New Castle of Manzanares el Real and had Juan Guas construct the Palacio del Infantado in Guadalajara.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married María de Luna y Pimentel, only surviving child and heiress of Álvaro de Luna, who had been his grandfather's greatest adversary. Through this marriage, he greatly expanded the wealth and possessions of the Mendoza famil
2 CONC y.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had three children :
2 CONT
2 CONT Diego Hurtado de Mendoza, 3rd Duke of the Infantado (1461-1531)
2 CONT
2 CONT Álvaro de Mendoza, 1st Lord of Torre de Esteban Hambrán
2 CONT
2 CONT Francisca de Mendoza, married Luis de la Cerda, Lord of Miedes and Mandayona
