2 CONT Íñigo Fernández de Velasco, 2nd Duke of Frías, Grandee of Spain, (in full, Spanish: Don Íñigo Fernández de Velasco y López de Mendoza, segundo duque de la villa de Frías, cuarto conde de Haro, octavo Condestable de Castilla, mayor
2 CONC azgo y señor de la Casa de Velasco, Caballero del Toisón de Oro), (1462–17 September 1528), was a Spanish nobleman and Duke of Frias.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fernández de Velasco was the son of Pedro Fernández de Velasco and of Mencía de Mendoza y Figueroa, and he inherited the titles from his older brother Bernardino, who had no legitimate male issue. He married María de Tovar, Lady o
2 CONC f Berlanga, with whom he had six children.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Pedro Fernández de Velasco, 3rd Duke of Frías
2 CONT
2 CONT  Juan Sancho de Tovar, 1st Marquis of Berlanga
2 CONT
2 CONT  Mencía de Velasco
2 CONT
2 CONT  María de Velasco, nun
2 CONT
2 CONT  Isabel de Velasco
2 CONT
2 CONT  Juana de Velasco, nun
2 CONT
2 CONT He took part in the Castilian War of the Communities, and led the royalist army to victory at the Battle of Villalar.
2 CONT
