1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (II) Señor de Bethencourt y de Saint Vincent de Rouvray, mencionado en diversos documentos comprendidos entre los años de 1278 a 1299. Fue también mencionado como Vizconde de Maulévrier.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Regnault de Bethencourt was born circa 1250 Sigy-en-Bray, Argueil, Dieppe, Seine-Maritime, France. He inherited from his father the lordship of Béthencourt and of Saint Vincent de Rouvray in 1278.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was appointed as viscount of Maulévrier in 1299.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died circa 1306 France.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 4. Regnault de Bethencourt (II) (Philippe, Jean) (suffix added for clarification)1,13,5,13,7,8,9,10,12 was also known as Reygnault Bethencourt.12 He was also known as Regnault de Béthencourt.11 He was also known as Renaud de Bette
2 CONC ncourt.7 He was also known as Regnault de Bettencourt (II).9 He was also known as Regnault de Bethancourt.16 He was born circa 1250 at Sigy-en-Bray, Argueil, Dieppe, Seine-Maritime, France.1,11,9 He inherited from his father the l
2 CONC ordship of Béthencourt and of Saint Vincent de Rouvray in 1278.1,13,14 He was referred to in various documents after 1280 at Sigy-en-Bray.1 In 1282 he is referred to in a Latin document as Lord of Bettencourt and of S. Vicente de 
2 CONC Rouvray.8 He was appointed as viscount of Maulévrier in 1299.1 He died circa 1306 at France.1,11
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Regnault de Bethencourt (II) include:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * +  5  i.   Jean de Bethencourt (I) was born between 1270 and 1280 at France. He married Nicole de Grainville at Caux, France. 
2 CONT
