1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Inigo de Argüello y Manrique was from Carrión de los Condes a municipality in the province of Palencia, part of the Autonomous Community of Castile and León, Spain.  Carrión de los Condes is 40 kilometers from the 
2 CONC town of Palencia and on the Camino de Santiago. Inigo went to Extremadura to help his kinsman Gabriel Fernandez Manrique, Conde de Osorio y Señor de Galisteo (Cáceres) in defense of his village.  Please see below for the family co
2 CONC nnection between Inigo de Argüello y Manrique and Gabriel Fernandez Manrique:
2 CONT
2 CONT Catalina de Carvajal 4th great grandfather Alfonso 'el Desheredado' de la Cerda de Castilla, electo rey de Castilla y León brother was Fernando de la Cerda de Castilla, señor de Lara who was the 4th great grandfather to Gabriel Fe
2 CONC rnández Manrique, I Duque de Galisteo y I Conde de Osorno.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catalina de Carvajal father was García López de Carvajal, I señor de Torrejón, oidor de la Chancillería de Valladolid y consejero de Juan II.
2 CONT
2 CONT García López de Carvajal, I señor de Torrejón, oidor de la Chancillería de Valladolid y consejero de Juan II mother was Mencía González de Carvajal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mencía González de Carvajal mother was Sevilla López de Villalobos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sevilla López de Villalobos mother was Inés de la Cerda, Señora de Bembibre.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inés de la Cerda, Señora de Bembibre father was Alfonso 'el Desheredado' de la Cerda de Castilla, electo rey de Castilla y León.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfonso 'el Desheredado' de la Cerda de Castilla, electo rey de Castilla y León brother was Fernando de la Cerda de Castilla, señor de Lara.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fernando de la Cerda de Castilla, señor de Lara son was Juan Nuñez de Lara Cerda, III Señor de Lara.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Nuñez de Lara Cerda, III Señor de Lara daughter was Juana de Lara, señora de Vizcaya y de Lara.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juana de Lara, señora de Vizcaya y de Lara son was Juan Téllez de Castilla, II señor de Aguilar de Campo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Téllez de Castilla, II señor de Aguilar de Campo daughter was Aldonza Téllez de Castilla, IV Señora de Aguilar De Campo y Castañeda.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aldonza Téllez de Castilla, IV Señora de Aguilar De Campo y Castañeda son was Gabriel Fernández Manrique, I Duque de Galisteo y I Conde de Osorno.
2 CONT
2 CONT Le Carrión de los Condes was taken from the Moors by Alonso Carreno between 791-842.  Don Carreno took the name Carrión.
2 CONT
2 CONT The town was inhabited by Jews at an early date.  Although they outnumbered the Christians both in numbers and in property, they submitted in 1126 to the victorious King Alfonso VI, who showed himself favorably disposed toward the
2 CONC m.  King Alfonso VI was the 9th great grandfather of Catalina de Carvajal, the wife of Inigo de Arguello y Manrique.
2 CONT
2 CONT King Alfonso Vi the Brave, King of Castile and Leon his sister Elvira Alfonso, Condessa de Tolosa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elvira Alfonso, Condessa de Tolosa her daughter Teresa Fernández de Villlalobos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Teresa Fernández de Villlalobos daughter Teresa Osorio, señora de Villalobos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Teresa Fernández de Villlalobos daughter Teresa Fernández de Castro y Osorio, Señora de Villalobos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Teresa Fernández de Castro y Osorio, Señora de Villalobos son Rodrigo Gil de Villalobos, señor de Villalobos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rodrigo Gil de Villalobos, señor de Villalobos son Rodrigo Gil de Villalobos, señor de Villalobos y Autillo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rodrigo Gil de Villalobos, señor de Villalobos y Autillo son Fernán Rodríguez de Villalobos, Señor de Villalobos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fernán Rodríguez de Villalobos, Señor de Villalobos daughter Sevilla López de Villalobos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sevilla López de Villalobos daughter Mencía González de Carvajal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mencía González de Carvajal son García López de Carvajal, I señor de Torrejón, oidor de la Chancillería de Valladolid y consejero de Juan II.
2 CONT
2 CONT García López de Carvajal, I señor de Torrejón, oidor de la Chancillería de Valladolid y consejero de Juan II daughter Catalina de Carvajal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catalina de Carvajal married to Inigo de Arguello y Manrique.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1160, many of the Jews settled in the neighboring city of Palencia.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Jewish community of Carrion was so large in 1290 that they paid 92,000 maravedis in taxes, not much less than the amount paid by the entire community of Burgos.  In Carrion, as elsewhere the Jews were persecuted.  Delegates fr
2 CONC om the city appeared before King Alfonso X of Castile, informing him that the Christians of the city, because of a groundless suspicion, had risen against the Jews and killed two of them; that thereupon the Jews had sought refuge 
2 CONC in the palace of the prince, who was absent at the time, and when the Christians followed in pursuit, had escaped through a secret door leading into the court, and locked their pursuers in.
