1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00534176&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antonio_Manrique_de_Lara,_2nd_Duke_of_N%C3%A1jera
2 CONT
2 CONT Antonio Manrique de Lara, 2nd Duke of Nájera (? - Navarrete, La Rioja, December 13, 1535) was a Spanish noble and military leader, and Viceroy of Navarre between 1516 and 1521.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the second son of Pedro Manrique de Lara, captain general of Army of Navarre and capitán general de la Frontera de Aragón, Navarra y Jaén. His mother was Guiomar de Castro.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father was named 1st Duke of Nájera by Ferdinand II of Aragon and Isabella I of Castile on August 30 1482. Antonio became second Duke in 1515, when his father died. He was also 3rd Count of Treviño.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1519 he was made a knight in the Order of the Golden Fleece by Charles I of Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Appointed viceroy of Navarre by Cardinal Cisneros in 1516, he was ordered to pacify the newly conquered Kingdom. But he acted in such a brutal manner, that he became much hated by the Navarrese. When the son of the former King of 
2 CONC Navarre, Henry II sent a large French/Navarrese army commanded by General André de Foix to reconquer his Kingdom, the Navarrese population supported them and in less than three weeks, all of Navarre was retaken.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1520 he participated in the repression of the Revolt of the Comuneros and in 1521 he defeated the French in the Siege of Logroño, and the Battle of Noáin.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the reconquest of the Kingdom by the Spanish, Antonio was sidelined and retired to his estates in La Rioja, where he died in 1535.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and children
2 CONT
2 CONT He married in 1503 with Juana Cardona Y Enriquez (died 1547), sister of Fernando Ramon Folch, 2nd Duke of Cardona.
2 CONT
2 CONT  They had seven children :
2 CONT
2 CONT  Juan Esteban (1504–1558), 3rd Duke of Nájera, knight in the Order of the Golden Fleece.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Aldonza, no issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Guiomar (died 1543), no issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Juan Fernandéz (1508–1570), viceroy of Naples in 1558, had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Rodrigo, had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT  María, no issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Bernardino (died 1591), had issue.
