1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedro_de_Est%C3%BA%C3%B1iga_y_Leiva
2 CONT
2 CONT =====
2 CONT Pedro de Zúñiga y Leiva († in 1453), 1st Count of Plasencia, 2nd Lord of Béjar, 1st Count of Ledesma (which he lost because he had to return it to its former owner the Infante Enrique of Aragon), 1st Count of Trujillo, (whom he re
2 CONC nounced in exchange for the County of Plasencia), Lord of Ayamonte, Miranda, etc. He married Isabel de Guzmán y Ayala, lady of Gibraleón.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He was succeeded by his son: Álvaro de Zúñiga y Guzmán († in 1488), 2nd Count of Plasencia, 3rd Lord of Béjar, 1st Duke of Arévalo, 1st Duke of Plasencia, 1st Count of Bañares, 1st Lord of Ayamonte, Gibraleón, etc. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The primitive county of Plasencia became extinct in 1476, when the Catholic Monarchs elevated this county to a duchy with the same name, in favor of Álvaro de Zúñiga y Guzmán, in compensation for the loss of the Duchy of Arévalo, 
2 CONC which reverted to the Crown.
2 CONT
2 CONT The title was revived by King Philip III who granted it to Pedro Lanuza y Ximénez de Urrea in 1611.
2 CONT
2 CONT  I	Pedro Lanuza y Ximénez de Urrea	1611-
2 CONT II	Ferrer de Lanuza y Silva	- 1643
2 CONT III	José de Lanuza y de Rocabertí	? -1688
2 CONT IV	Juan de Lanuza y de Oms	? -1723
2 CONT V	Francisco de Lanuza y de Gilabert	
2 CONT VI	Juan Antonio de Lanuza y de Boxadors	? -1770
2 CONT VII	María Helena de Lanuza y de Boxadors	? -1806
2 CONT VIII	Josefa Rabasa de Perellós y Lanuza	
2 CONT IX	María Dolores de Marimón Queri	
2 CONT X	José María de Arróspide y Marimón	? -1893
2 CONT XI	José María de Arróspide y Álvarez	1893-1936
2 CONT XII	Francisco de Arróspide y Arróspide	
2 CONT XIII	Íñigo de Arróspide y Valera	-1983
2 CONT XIV	Álvaro de Arróspide y López de Letona	1983-2012
2 CONT XV	Cristina de Arróspide y Núñez - 2012- until now
2 CONT
2 CONT Taken from:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Condado_de_Plasencia
2 CONT
