1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =='''John Sutton V==
2 CONT '''Sir John de Sutton V (February 1380 – 28 August 1406)[1] was the 4th Baron Sutton of Dudley[2] and heir to Dudley Castle. He was the son of''' Sir John de Sutton IV, 3rd Baron Sutton, and Joan[3] (d.1408).[2] '''John married Co
2 CONC nstance Blount (d.11 October 1432),[4] daughter of''' Sir Walter le Blount of Barton who was killed at the Battle of Shrewsbury in c.1402, whose death was immortalized by Shakespear.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John V is a descendant of the first Lord Dudley,''' Sir John de Sutton II (c.1310–1359) the first to be summoned to the Parliament of England as Baron Sutton in 1342.[6] '''From 1397 to 1406, John V held lands derived from the 
2 CONC Earls of Powis, upon the death of his great grandmother'''[2] Isabel de Cherleton. '''In 1401, during the second year of King Henry IV of England's reign, John V did homage for the lands, including Castle Dudley.[7][4] After John 
2 CONC V's death, the Blounts had a stake in Dudley lands when his mother-in-law''', Donna Sanchia de Ayala (d.1418),[8] '''took custody of his first child''' John VI,[9][10] who was age six, as well as being granted John V's valuable es
2 CONC tates.[11] Widowed, Constance was eventually sued by Robert Erghom for her dower in the King's chancery by which she defaulted several times on the King's grant of Dudley manor.[12]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John V was succeeded by''' John Sutton VI, 1st Baron Dudley. '''By Constance, his other children included''' Thomas Sutton of Dudley, and Elizabeth Sutton of Dudley.[13] '''He is also said to have had a child''', Humphrey Dudle
2 CONC y.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_de_Sutton_V
2 CONT *___________________________
2 CONT *'''Sir John V Sutton, Lord Dudley1,2,3,4,5
2 CONT *'''M, #11188, b. February 1380, d. 28 August 1406
2 CONT *Father      Sir John de Sutton6,5 b. 6 Dec 1362, d. 10 Mar 1396
2 CONT *Mother     Alice le Despenser6,5 b. c 1369
2 CONT *'''     Sir John V Sutton, Lord Dudley was born in February 1380 at of Dudley, Sedgeley, Kingswinford, & Rowley-Somery, Staffordshire, England; Age 17 in 1397, & 21 in 1401.2,3,5 He married Constance Blount, daughter of Sir Walte
2 CONC r Blount and Sancha de Ayala, before 10 December 1401; They had 2 sons (Sir John, 1st Lord Dudley; & Thomas).2,3,4,5 Sir John V Sutton, Lord Dudley died on 28 August 1406 at Dudley Castle, Dudley, Staffordshire, England, at age 26
2 CONC .3,5
2 CONT *'''Family      Constance Blount d. 23 Sep 1432
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Sir John Sutton, 1st Lord Dudley, 4th Baron Dudley+7,8,3,4,5 b. 25 Dec 1400, d. 30 Sep 1487
2 CONT **Hamon Sutton+ b. c 1402
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S2950] Unknown author, The Complete Peerage, by Cokayne, Vol. IV, p. 479; Ancestors of American Presidents by Gary Boyd Roberts, p. 149; Plantagenet Ancestry of 17th Century Colonists, by David Faris, p. 90; Burke's Peerage, 
2 CONC 1938, p. 857.
2 CONT * 2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 277.
2 CONT * 3.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. IV, p. 153.
2 CONT * 4.[S6] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry: 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 668-669.
2 CONT * 5.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. V, p. 101.
2 CONT * 6.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. IV, p. 152-153.
2 CONT * 7.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 277-278.
2 CONT * 8.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 276.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p373.htm#i11188
2 CONT *___________________
2 CONT *'''Sir John de Sutton1
2 CONT *'''M, #2647, b. circa 1380, d. 29 August 1406
2 CONT *Last Edited=20 Oct 2009
2 CONT *'''     Sir John de Sutton was born circa 1380.1 He was the son of Sir John de Sutton and Alice le Despencer.1 He married Constance Blount, daughter of Sir Walter Blount and Sancha de Ayala, before 10 December 1401.2 He died on 2
2 CONC 9 August 1406.1
2 CONT *'''     He lived at Dudley Castle, Staffordshire, England.1
2 CONT *'''Child of Sir John de Sutton and Constance Blount
2 CONT ** 1.John Sutton, 1st Lord Dudley+1 b. 25 Dec 1400, d. 30 Sep 1487
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] BP2003 volume 1, page 1191. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT * 2.[S37] BP2003. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p265.htm#i2647
2 CONT *__________________
2 CONT *'''John SUTTON
2 CONT *'''Born: 1379
2 CONT *'''Died: 1407
2 CONT *Father: John SUTTON
2 CONT *Mother: Alice (Joan) DESPENCER
2 CONT *'''Married: Constance BLOUNT ABT 1400, Worcestershire, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. John SUTTON (1º B. Sutton of Dudley)
2 CONT **2. Thomas SUTTON
2 CONT **3. Humphrey SUTTON
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/SUTTON.htm#John SUTTON2
2 CONT *__________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT John Sutton V, (1380--29 August 1406) was born at Coleshill, Warwickshire, the son of John Sutton IV (1361-1395), of Dudley Castle who wed Alice de Spencer of Carlington. John Sutton IV was the son of John Sutton III, (1339-c.1370
2 CONC ) and Catherine de Stafford (1340-1361). Catherine was the daughter of Ralph Stafford, 1st Earl of Stafford and Margaret de Audley.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John - Son and heir of Dudley Castle, co. Stafford, was born in Feb 1380 (aged seventeen years and three weeks on death of father), or a few days before 23 Mar 1379/80 (inquest into his inheritance from his great-grandmother I
2 CONC sabel). 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1401 he did homage and had livery of the Barony of Dudley and other family lands (the first time they had been vested in a male heir since the death of his great-grandfather in 1359).
2 CONT
2 CONT John Sutton V married to Constance, the daughter of Walter Blount and Sancha de Ayala, the daughter of Diego Gomez de Toledo, mayor of Toledo. Their son was the first lord Dudley, who bore the same name.
2 CONT
2 CONT ID: I52450  Name: JOHN De Sutton Dudley  Given Name: JOHN De Sutton  Surname: Dudley  Suffix: V  Sex: M  Birth: Feb 1379-1380 in Coleshill, Arden, Warwickshire, England  Christening: Dudley, Warwickshire, England  Death: 29 Aug 14
2 CONC 06 in England  Change Date: 21 Sep 2005 at 15:22
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: John De Sutton b: 6 Dec 1361 in Coleshill, Warwickshire, England  Mother: Alice (Joan) Despenser b: Abt 1364 in Carlington, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Constance-Constantine Blount b: 1380 in Barton, Blount, Burton-upon-Trent, Derbyshire, England Married: Bef 1396 in Worcestershire, England  Change Date: 9 Oct 2005 Children
2 CONT  JOHN VI Sutton b: 25 Dec 1400 in Dudley Castle, Staffordshire, England c: in Barton, Derbyshire, England
2 CONT  Hamon Sutton b: Abt 1396
2 CONT
2 CONT References Burkes Peerage and Baronetage (1939), s.v. Dudley  Information on Sir John Sutton from R. B. Stewart of My Lines 
2 CONT *__________________________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical history of the dormant, abeyant, forfeited, and extinct ... By Sir Bernard Burke
2 CONT *http://archive.org/details/agenealogicalhi00burkgoog
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=1ysWkXKSrpIC&pg=PA55&lpg=PA55&dq=Thomas+LEIGH+1509&source=bl&ots=K8gUSCKlcI&sig=eL9fXqb38lIHsWmx_nK8bu_77j8&hl=en&ei=h60CTuXdMYP4sAOg38mIBA&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=4&ved=0CCsQ6AEwAzgU
2 CONC #v=onepage&q=Thomas%20LEIGH%201509&f=false
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/agenealogicalhi00burkgoog#page/n74/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.54
2 CONT *SIR WALTER BLOUNT, so celebrated for his martial prowess in
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/agenealogicalhi00burkgoog#page/n75/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg. 55
2 CONT *the warlike times of EDWARD III., RICHARD II., and HENRY IV., and immortalized by the muse of Shakespeare for his devotion, even unto death, to King HENRY. Sir Walter fell at the battle of Shrewsbury, 22 June, 1403, .... etc.
2 CONT * .... By his wife, Donna Sancha, who survived him, and lived until 1418, he left issue,
2 CONT **I. JOHN (Sir), his heir, one of the great warriors who have immortalized the reign and times of HENRY V.
2 CONT **II. THOMAS (Sir), successor to his brother.
2 CONT **III. James (Sir), who m. Anne, dau. of Roger Parker, Esq., of Lillinghall, and was father of Roger Blount, of Grendon, ancestor of the BLOUNTS of Grendon, Eldersfield, Orleton, &c.; the present male representative of the BLOUNTS
2 CONC  of Orleton, co Herefore, is WILLIAM BLOUNT, Esq., of that place.
2 CONT **IV. Peter, d.s.p.
2 CONT **'''I. Constantia, m. to John Sutton, Lord Dudley.
2 CONT **II. Anne, m. to Thomas Griffith, of Wichnor, co. Salop, living in 1415.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *__________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT John Sutton Vth, (b. 1380, Coleshill, Warwickshire d. 1406). Married to Constance, the daughter of Walter Blount. Marriage performed by Sancha de Ayala, the daughter of Diego Gomez de Toledo, mayor of Toledo.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Sutton V was the father of the first lord Dudley, who bore the same name.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Sutton Vth's father was John Sutton IV (1361-1395), of Dudley Castle who wed Alice de Spencer of Carlington.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is widely held that John Sutton IV was the son of John Sutton III, (1339-1370) and Catherine de Stafford (1340-1361). Catherine was the daughter of Ralph Stafford, 1st Earl of Stafford and Margaret de Audley.
2 CONT *________________________
