1 NOTE Katarina av Aragonien
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=image&guid=0b8afdb1-2abe-4a6c-8b11-89c008f6a952&tid=9342424&pid=-411687246
1 NOTE Allm&#228;nt
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=c3e03d29-4688-474c-98df-ff8f5f5bd36d&tid=9342424&pid=-411687246
1 NOTE Catherine of Aragon was a Spanish princess (her badge shows a pomegranate - a symbol from Spain).
2 CONT               She was the daughter of King Ferdinand and Queen Isabella of Spain, and was originally married to
2 CONT               Henry's brother Arthur. Henry married Catherine to maintain the alliance with Spain after Arthur died,
2 CONT               leaving Catherine a widow. This marriage was organized by Henry VII a short time before he died, but
2 CONT               took place after his death in 1509, when Henry was almost 18 and Catherine was 23.
2 CONT
2 CONT               After twenty years of marriage, she had only given birth to one girl, Mary, later to become known as Bloody Mary (although she had many miscarriages and still-births in that time). As Henry VIII needed a son to provi
2 CONC de a male heir to the throne, and as his advisors deemed Catherine to be past the age of child-birth, Henry tried to persuade her to become a Nun. Catherine refused, and after two years of arguments with the Pope, Henry
2 CONT  created a new Archbishop (Thomas Cranmer) who was prepared to declare the marriage
2 CONT  annulled in 1532. Catherine was then banished from the Court and separated from her daughter.
2 CONT  It is said that she died of a broken heart, four years later.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.larmouth.demon.co.uk/sarah-jayne/wives/wives.html
1 NOTE Catherine of Aragon
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=image&guid=38a4947d-4748-42cb-aa4d-cb58490eb023&tid=822673&pid=-1379463149
1 NOTE AKA, Catherina de Hapsburg
1 NOTE OR "CATALINA""OF ARAGON"
1 NOTE Catherine of Aragon (1485-1536), first wife of Henry VIII of England, the youngest child of Ferdinand and Isabella of Spain. Consult Hume�s Wives of Henry VIII. [World Wide Illustrated Encyclopedia, 1935]
2 CONT Kept under house arrest at Kimbolton after her divorce from Henry, where she died. She had previously been married for several months to his older brother Arthur who died before he could inherit the throne. The marriage with Henry
2 CONC  lasted for 24 years during which she was pregnant several times, their first child was born dead and a son born in 1511 died after ten days. Only Mary Tudor, later Queen, survived. When Catherine was in her forties and past child
2 CONC  bearing Henry divorced her. [THELMA.GED]
1 NOTE Posthumousley Catherine of Aragon
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=image&guid=e79a7967-564e-4e5f-b5dd-4197dbd9faa3&tid=822673&pid=-1379463149
1 NOTE     Line 2827 from GEDCOM File not recognizable or too long:
2 CONT     NAME Catalina (Catherine) Queen Of /ENGLAND/
2 CONT     Line 2828 from GEDCOM File not recognizable or too long:
2 CONT     TITL PRINCESS OF ARAGON
2 CONT     Line 2828 from GEDCOM File not recognizable or too long:
2 CONT     TITL PRINCESS OF ARAGON
2 CONT     From Ancestral File (TM), data as of 5 JAN 1998.
1 NOTE She, as the first wife of King Henry VIII, occupies a prominent place in 
2 CONT history because the question of her marriage to Henry was a factor in the 
2 CONT Reformation in England.  Henry's father, King Henry VII, hoped to form a 
2 CONT binding alliance with Spain when he negotiated the marriage of Catherine 
2 CONT and his son Arthur, prince of Wales. She went to England in 1501 and was 
2 CONT married in November, but Arthur died in April 1502. A few months later 
2 CONT Henry VII arranged a second marriage for Catherine with his second son 
2 CONT Henry, then 12 years old. A papal dispensation enabling Henry to marry the 
2 CONT widow of his brother was obtained in 1503. Henry succeeded to the throne 
2 CONT in April 1509 and in June he married Catherine. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Although the marriage was, on the whole, fairly successful, the 
2 CONT pro-Spanish sympathies of Catherine brought some difficulties during the 
2 CONT periods of French alliance. Catherine bore Henry six children, only one of 
2 CONT whom, a daughter, later Queen Mary I, survived. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1527 Henry tried to annul his marriage to Catherine so that he could 
2 CONT marry Anne Boleyn, who he hoped would give him a male heir to the throne. 
2 CONT The pope refused to make a decision on the proposed annulment, and in 1533 
2 CONT Henry was married to Anne by the archbishop of Canterbury. In 1534 the 
2 CONT pope finally declared that the first marriage was valid, thus bringing 
2 CONT about the alienation of Henry VIII from the Roman Catholic church. 
2 CONT Catherine did not quit the kingdom, but was thereafter closely guarded. 
2 CONT During this time she displayed heroic courage and steadfastly refused to 
2 CONT sign away her rights and those of Mary.
1 NOTE Young Catherine of Aragon
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=image&guid=79decddb-12ce-477e-9205-0fc8c65822d4&tid=822673&pid=-1379463149
