1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bartolom%C3%A9_de_las_Casas
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bartolom%C3%A9_de_las_Casas
2 CONT
2 CONT Bartolomé de las Casas O.P. (c. 1484[1] – 18 July 1566) was a 16th-century Spanish historian, social reformer and Dominican friar. He became the first resident Bishop of Chiapas, and the first officially appointed "Protector of th
2 CONC e Indians". His extensive writings, the most famous being "A Short Account of the Destruction of the Indies" and "Historia de Las Indias", chronicle the first decades of colonization of the West Indies, focusing particularly on th
2 CONC e atrocities committed by the colonizers against the Indigenous peoples
2 CONT ==================================
2 CONT Bartholomew de las Casas; his life, his apostolate, and his writings (1909)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Author: MacNutt, Francis Augustus, 1863-1927
2 CONT  Subject: Casas, Bartolomé de las, 1474-1566
2 CONT  Publisher: New York, London, G. P. Putnam's sons
2 CONT  Language: English
2 CONT
